      "widgets_values": [
        "## FLUX.1 Krea [dev] GGUF \u2014 Full Quality Pipeline\n\nBase gen (1024\u00b2, 28 steps) \u2192 4x ESRGAN upscale \u2192 downscale to 2048\u00b2 \u2192 hires-fix pass (16 steps, denoise 0.5) \u2192 final save.\n\n### Models needed\n- `unet/flux1-krea-dev-Q4_K_S.gguf`\n- `text_encoders/clip_l.safetensors`\n- `text_encoders/t5xxl_fp8_e4m3fn.safetensors`\n- `vae/ae.safetensors`\n- `upscale_models/4x-UltraSharp.pth` (reused from Klein setup)\n\n### Requires custom node\nComfyUI-GGUF (city96) \u2014 for the UnetLoaderGGUF node. Install via Manager.\n\n### Key difference from Klein 4B\nKrea [dev] is NOT distilled \u2014 it uses real CFG (set to 4.0 here) and the negative prompt actually matters. This is a standard KSampler, not the Flux2 guider chain.\n\n### Settings\n- CFG 4.0 on both passes (try 3.5\u20135 range)\n- Pass 1: 28 steps, native 1024\u00b2\n- Pass 2 (hires-fix): 16 steps, denoise 0.5, at 2048\u00b2\n- Sampler: euler / simple\n\n### License\nFLUX.1 [dev] Non-Commercial License \u2014 personal/research use only.\n\n### 6GB VRAM note\nLaunch ComfyUI with `--lowvram`. The T5 text encoder (4.89GB) plus the GGUF model means tighter headroom than Klein \u2014 if you OOM, add `--cpu-vae` or drop to Q3_K_M (5.37GB) quant instead."
      ],
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    }
